---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Playbook for America">
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pt-24 pb-16">
    <header class="mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-5xl text-p4a-bg1 font-bold font-serif">Playbook for America</h1>
      <p class="text-2xl font-serif font-light">An independent, nonpartisan, and practical civic platform</p>
    </header>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-p4a-bg1 font-serif font-bold mb-4">Our Mission</h2>
      <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        The Playbook for America (P4A) exists to bring together ideas and programs that improve government, strengthen democracy, and renew civic life in the United States.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        Organized as a nonpartisan nonprofit, P4A operates an online platform where citizens and government officials can crowdsource, discuss, and rank ideas and programs, with a focus on turning the most promising ones into actionable solutions. Our aim is to elevate the best ideas from all corners of the nation and help move them toward real-world impact.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-p4a-bg1 font-serif font-bold mb-4">Our Vision</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        We envision a United States where public policy is shaped by the collective intelligence of its people, government institutions are more effective and trusted, and civic life is active, inclusive, and constructive. In this future, citizens and public servants work together to identify shared priorities, translate ideas into meaningful improvements at home, and help the United States play a responsible role in addressing shared global challenges while making the world a better place.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-p4a-bg1 font-serif font-bold mb-4">Our Values</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        P4A is grounded in a commitment to nonpartisanship, openness, and respect for diverse perspectives. We believe the best ideas can come from anywhere, that constructive dialogue is essential to a healthy democracy, and that transparency and fairness are critical to building trust. We value collaboration between citizens and government, and we are guided by a focus on practical, evidence-informed solutions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="mb-8 mt-12 text-center">
      <a
        href="https://airtable.com/appH0YK3BFKCCfUVB/pagERE8ylQTG39EZN/form"
        target="_blank"
        class="inline-block"
      >
        <button class="bg-p4a-bg1 hover:bg-p4a-bg2 text-white font-bold px-36 py-4 rounded shadow-lg">
          Share your perspective
        </button>
      </a>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 ">4-minute survey · Optional email for updates or involvement</p>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-p4a-bg1 font-serif font-bold mb-4">Founders Backstory</h2>
      <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Most Americans want to improve government, strengthen democracy, renew civic life, and contribute to a healthier role for the United States in the world. Many would participate more actively if there were a safe, fair environment where people could share, discuss, and rank ideas—and help the best ones take root and drive real-world impact.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        I'm <a class="underline text-p4a-bg1 hover:text-p4a-bg2" href="https://linkedin.com/in/jknapp" target="_blank">John Knapp</a> and this is a project I'm kicking off. I build software, especially software that helps people improve their lives and their communities. Three simple truths motivate my effort: most people agree America could be in better shape; many Americans have ideas about how to get there; and if people don't feel they have a voice—or believe they can be heard—they disengage. That would be a loss for all of us.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        I encourage your partcipation.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
